<h1>Casino Cost Calculator</h1>

<p>House edge sounds small until you apply it to the amount of money actually moving across the table. Enter your bet size, pace, and playing time to estimate the long-run mathematical cost of a casino wager.</p>

<div class="calc-card" id="costCalc">
  <div class="calc-row">
    <label for="calcGame">Game / bet</label>
    <select id="calcGame">
      <option value="crapsOdds" data-edge="0.00">Craps Odds — 0%</option>
      <option value="crapsDontPass" data-edge="{{ odds.houseEdgeStr.dontPass }}">Craps Don't Pass — {{ odds.houseEdgeStr.dontPass }}%</option>
      <option value="crapsPassLine" data-edge="{{ odds.houseEdgeStr.passLine }}">Craps Pass Line — {{ odds.houseEdgeStr.passLine }}%</option>
      <option value="baccaratBanker" data-edge="{{ baccaratOdds.houseEdge.banker }}">Baccarat Banker — {{ baccaratOdds.houseEdge.banker }}%</option>
      <option value="baccaratPlayer" data-edge="{{ baccaratOdds.houseEdge.player }}">Baccarat Player — {{ baccaratOdds.houseEdge.player }}%</option>
      <option value="baccaratTie" data-edge="{{ baccaratOdds.houseEdge.tie }}">Baccarat Tie — {{ baccaratOdds.houseEdge.tie }}%</option>
      <option value="europeanRoulette" data-edge="2.70">European Roulette — 2.70%</option>
      <option value="americanRoulette" data-edge="{{ rouletteOdds.houseEdge.standard }}" selected>American Roulette — {{ rouletteOdds.houseEdge.standard }}%</option>
      <option value="americanRouletteFiveNumber" data-edge="{{ rouletteOdds.houseEdge.topLine }}">American Roulette Five-Number Bet — {{ rouletteOdds.houseEdge.topLine }}%</option>
      <option value="blackjack" data-edge="0.5">Blackjack — ~0.5% with good rules/basic strategy</option>
    </select>
  </div>
  <div class="calc-row">
    <label for="calcBetAmt">Average bet ($)</label>
    <input id="calcBetAmt" type="number" min="1" step="1" value="25" inputmode="numeric">
  </div>
  <div class="calc-row">
    <label for="calcBetsHr">Bets / hands / spins per hour</label>
    <input id="calcBetsHr" type="number" min="1" step="1" value="50" inputmode="numeric">
  </div>
  <div class="calc-row">
    <label for="calcHours">Hours played</label>
    <input id="calcHours" type="number" min="0.5" step="0.5" value="3" inputmode="decimal">
  </div>
  <div class="calc-result" id="costResult" aria-live="polite"></div>
</div>

<p>Blackjack's house edge depends entirely on the specific table rules and whether you're playing correct basic strategy — 0.5% is a commonly cited approximate figure for good rules, not a universal constant the way it is for the other bets above.</p>

<script>
(function () {
  function fmt(n) { return '$' + n.toFixed(2); }

  function render() {
    var select = document.getElementById('calcGame');
    var edge = parseFloat(select.selectedOptions[0].getAttribute('data-edge'));
    var bet = parseFloat(document.getElementById('calcBetAmt').value);
    var betsHr = parseFloat(document.getElementById('calcBetsHr').value);
    var hours = parseFloat(document.getElementById('calcHours').value);
    var out = document.getElementById('costResult');

    if (!bet || bet <= 0 || !betsHr || betsHr <= 0 || !hours || hours <= 0 || isNaN(edge)) {
      out.innerHTML = '<p class="calc-note">Enter a bet size, pace, and hours played, all above 0.</p>';
      return;
    }

    var totalAction = bet * betsHr * hours;
    var expectedCost = totalAction * edge / 100;
    var perHour = bet * betsHr * edge / 100;

    var lines = [];
    lines.push('<div class="calc-line"><span>Total action</span><b>' + fmt(totalAction) + '</b></div>');
    lines.push('<div class="calc-line"><span>House edge</span><b>' + edge.toFixed(2) + '%</b></div>');
    lines.push('<div class="calc-line calc-line-lg"><span>Theoretical expected cost</span><b>' + fmt(expectedCost) + '</b></div>');
    lines.push('<div class="calc-line"><span>Expected cost per hour</span><b>' + fmt(perHour) + '</b></div>');

    out.innerHTML = lines.join('') + '<p class="calc-note">This is a long-run mathematical expectation, not a prediction of what you will lose in one session. Short-term results can vary dramatically.</p>';
  }

  document.getElementById('calcGame').addEventListener('change', render);
  document.getElementById('calcBetAmt').addEventListener('input', render);
  document.getElementById('calcBetsHr').addEventListener('input', render);
  document.getElementById('calcHours').addEventListener('input', render);
  render();
})();
</script>

<h2>What does "expected cost" mean?</h2>

<p>Expected cost is total amount wagered × house edge. A 5.26% house edge does not mean you will lose 5.26% of your bankroll every session. It means that over a very large number of wagers, the casino theoretically retains about $5.26 for every $100 of total action.</p>

